    "teach_4": {
      "id": "teach_4",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "What does 6 ÷ 3/4 mean?\n\nIt asks: how many pieces of size 3/4 fit into 6?\n\nEach whole holds 4/3 of such a piece... easier way:\n\nDividing by a fraction = multiplying by it flipped upside down.\n\n6 ÷ 3/4 = 6 × 4/3 = 8",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_4_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_4_step": {
      "id": "teach_4_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The flipped fraction is called the reciprocal.\n\n3/4 ↔ 4/3\n\nSo:\n\n4/5 ÷ 8/15\n= 4/5 × 15/8\n= 60/40\n= 3/2\n\nFlip the second fraction, never the first.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_4"
        }
      ]
    },
